    "interpretation": "The city survey Photograph 1 shows stairs on the viewer’s left and the two-storey bay on the right. The attic pediment spans both. The bay occupies approximately 55% of the facade. Equal plan offsets produce 45-degree bay cheeks. The apparent gable rise is roughly half the eave width; the model follows the photographed near-45-degree pitch. These are photographic estimates. A fit to both slopes of all six long roofs using the 2023 USGS survey returns approximately 41–49 degrees (median 44). The continuous main roofs use 44 degrees with a 0.95 m fascia.",
